  "identifier": "cdisc-adam",
  "name": "CDISC ADaM",
  "alternateName": [
    "Analysis Data Model",
    "ADaM",
    "CDISC ADaM v1.3"
  ],
  "description": "The CDISC standard for analysis-ready clinical trial datasets — the layer between raw SDTM tabulation data and the statistical analyses submitted to regulators. ADaM defines dataset structures and naming conventions that make it straightforward to trace every analysis result back to the source SDTM records (traceability). Core dataset types include ADSL (subject-level analysis dataset), ADAE (adverse events), ADLB (laboratory), ADTTE (time-to-event), and ADRS (response). Required by FDA and EMA alongside SDTM for new regulatory submissions. ADaM datasets are what statisticians and programmers build to produce the tables, listings, and figures (TLFs) in a clinical study report. ADaM Implementation Guides extend the model for specific endpoints — overall survival, PK, ECG, etc. Maintained by CDISC. Current version: ADaM v1.3 (2021). Companion to SDTM: SDTM = how trial data is collected and tabulated; ADaM = how it is analysed.",
  "url": "https://www.cdisc.org/standards/foundational/adam",
